Third-party material
--------------------
The MIT license above covers only the code and documentation written for this
project. Except as noted below, third-party code is not included in this
repository; it is fetched at build or install time and keeps its own license:
ESP-IDF, esp_codec_dev and esp_websocket_client (Apache License 2.0, Espressif
Systems), and the Python packages listed in pyproject.toml (each under its own
license).

Optional Linux audio uses python-sounddevice (MIT, Matthias Geier) and the
system PortAudio library (MIT). Raspberry Pi controls use GPIO Zero
(BSD-3-Clause) and the system lgpio library (Unlicense). These dependencies are
installed separately; their packages carry their respective license texts.
The optional Linux display uses pygame (LGPL 2.1) and SDL2 (zlib), also
installed separately. No pygame or SDL source is copied into this repository.

The optional MQTT example uses Eclipse Paho MQTT Python, dual licensed under
Eclipse Public License 2.0 and Eclipse Distribution License 1.0. It is installed
separately; its package includes both license texts. No Paho source is copied
into this repository.

assets/mascot/nous-girl-white-1024.png, the mascot bitmaps generated from it
(firmware/core/src/mascot_data.cpp) and the project logo derived from it
(docs/images/logo.png) are based on artwork from the Hermes Agent repository,
https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent, released under the MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research.

The CO5300 panel start-up commands in firmware/esp32/main/port_amoled.cpp (the
register values and their order) follow Waveshare's board support package for
the ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75,
https://components.espressif.com/components/waveshare/esp32_s3_touch_amoled_1_75,
released by Waveshare under the Apache License 2.0. A copy of that license is in
LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

The BOX-3 panel initialization register values in
firmware/esp32/main/panel_box3.hpp follow Espressif's ESP32-S3-BOX-3 BSP,
https://github.com/espressif/esp-bsp/tree/master/bsp/esp-box-3,
Copyright 2022-2026 Espressif Systems (Shanghai) CO LTD, Apache License 2.0.
The adapter changes sleep-out and display-on to zero data bytes and explicit
delays, and omits the legacy table terminator.

The CoreS3 ILI9342E initialization table in firmware/esp32/main/panel_cores3.hpp
is adapted from Espressif's m5stack_core_s3 BSP,
https://github.com/espressif/esp-bsp/tree/master/bsp/m5stack_core_s3,
Copyright 2026 Espressif Systems (Shanghai) CO LTD, Apache License 2.0.
The adapter expresses the register payloads as C++ byte strings and uses
zero-length sleep-out and display-on commands with explicit delays.

The managed esp_lcd_ili9341, esp_lcd_touch, esp_lcd_touch_gt911,
esp_lcd_touch_tt21100 and esp_lcd_touch_ft5x06 drivers are Espressif components
under Apache License 2.0. CoreS3 audio uses esp_codec_dev's AW88298 driver.
They are fetched at build time. Binary release packages include the installed
component and ESP-IDF license files alongside this notice.

The T-Display-S3 ST7789 initialization values and AW9364 backlight control in
firmware/esp32/main/port_parallel.cpp follow Xinyuan-LilyGO's factory example,
https://github.com/Xinyuan-LilyGO/T-Display-S3/blob/ec889e789b3cf093412689a143f7f37b42b56af7/examples/factory/factory.ino,
Copyright (c) 2022 Xinyuan-LilyGO, MIT License.
The adapter uses ESP-IDF GPIO and panel APIs, bounds brightness to 16 levels,
protects pulse timing, and uses explicit microsecond delays for backlight reset
and startup. The panel command lengths are stored separately from their values.
The full upstream license is in LICENSES/LilyGO-MIT.txt.

Branch customizations for the Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-2.16 (branch
`216-board`, by 0xjiangjiang)
--------------------------------------------------------------
Added: the esp32s3-touch-amoled-216 board profile (CO5300 QSPI panel with
MADCTL 0xA0 rotation, CST9220 touch mapping, AXP2101 ALDO3 display supply),
a GB2312 screen font (firmware/core/src/font_cjk.cpp, generated by
firmware/core/tools/gen_cjk_font.py), ESP-SR wake-word integration
(port_wakeword.cpp),
board-specific microphone gain / VAD tuning, default volume 100 and a
screen-always-on option, plus a Chinese flashing guide
(docs/local-flash-216.zh-CN.md). These additions are offered under the same
MIT License as upstream, with upstream copyright retained.

The CJK bitmap data in firmware/core/src/font_cjk.cpp is derived from
Noto Sans CJK SC (Copyright The Noto Project Authors, SIL Open Font License
1.1); the full OFL text is in docs/licenses/OFL-1.1.txt. The Noto font
itself is not included in this repository - only bitmap outlines rendered
from it at build-script time, used under OFL.

Pin mapping and power-rail facts for the 2.16 board were cross-checked
against the open-source AgentTouch firmware
(https://github.com/wentong2022-arch/agenttouch); no source is copied.

Wake-word models (wn9_xiaoaitongxue, wn9_nihaoxiaozhi_tts) are Espressif
esp-sr binaries fetched at build time via the managed-components registry;
they are not redistributed in this repository's source tree and remain under
Espressif's esp-sr license. "Waveshare" is a trademark of its owner; this is
an independent community port, not affiliated with or endorsed by Waveshare.
